,{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:23:04-07:00","id":149788,"title":"","content":"Yeah all three:<br /> Matrix<br /> Animatrix<br /> and<br /> The 13th floor<br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","user":"Eadee","date":". 05-26-2014, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T21:44:51-07:00","id":154509,"title":"","content":"This one just came to me.<br /> <br /> CyberSix: A Promethean on the run/fighting against the Technocracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:42:11-07:00","id":154822,"title":"","content":"Seriously... noone mentioned Penny Dreadful yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T08:30:32-07:00","id":154846,"title":"","content":"Marvel's Agents of SHIELD is extremely Technocrat. I saw about three episodes before I gave into temptation and started running a Techno game called 'A Magical Place'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T15:37:34-07:00","id":156942,"title":"","content":"I actually have a difficult time <i>not</i> seeing World of Darkness parallels/inspiration/theme in things I watch. Movies/TV shows I consider WoD as a whole, rather than just certain scenes or characters would include:<ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0414993/\" target=\"_blank\">The Fountain</a><br /> Werewolf and Mage, especially themes of ancestors/past lives, Mnesis, Umbral quests, or a Seeking. Huge inspiration for Theurges with their theme of death and rebirth, and the necessity of cycles.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1071804/?ref_=sr_3\" target=\"_blank\">Ink</a><br /> Werewolf and Changeling. Umbral Realms, dealing with Banes, being a Theurge. Could also be seen from the perspective of a Fomori being redeemed.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0765443/?ref_=sr_1\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Promises</a><br /> Werewolf. Shadow Lord / Kinfolk.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0424136/?ref_=sr_1\" target=\"_blank\">Hard Candy</a><br /> Werewolf. Black Fury / Kinfolk, incredibly Ragabash. Could also be good inspiration for a Nuwisha.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120657/?ref_=sr_1\" target=\"_blank\">The 13th Warrior</a><br /> Werewolf. The obligatory Silent-Strider-joins-a-pack-of-Fenrir-on-a-quest. There's even great Auspice role representation.</li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1119644/\" target=\"_blank\">Fringe</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mage. A more Technocratic world - or possibly Glass Walkers and the Mirror Zone!</span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0360486/\" target=\"_blank\">Constantine</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hunters, and Mortals with Hedge Magic and/or Numina</span>.</li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1856010/\" target=\"_blank\">House of Cards</a></span><br /> Vampire. Ridiculously Ventrue. (Bonus Corax reporter.)</li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0119698/\" target=\"_blank\">Princess Mononoke</a></span><br /> Werewolf. Themes of Weaver encroachment on the Wyld, Wyrm taint and corruption, spirits.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0756683/\" target=\"_blank\">The Man From Earth</a><br /> Werewolf, Vampire.Themes of immortality that could easily translate into Mnesis as well.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0366780/\" target=\"_blank\">MirrorMask</a><br /> Werewolf, Mage, Changeling. For similar reasons as Ink. Umbral realms, the Umbra in general.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0433362/\" target=\"_blank\">Daybreakers</a><br /> Vampire. An actual vampire flick, too! Sam Neill is excellent.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1438176/\" target=\"_blank\">Fright Night</a><br /> Vampire. Another intentionally vampire movie. I can't help but think of some Sabbat Lasombra out for entertainment.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0298228/\" target=\"_blank\">Whale Rider</a><br /> Werewolf, maybe Mage. Lots of good mythos, prophecy, and spirituality themes. Made me think of Kinfolk.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0499549/\" target=\"_blank\">Avatar</a><br /> Werewolf. Pandora is such a great representation of an Umbral realm, and a living, vital Gaia. Mnesis themes, animistic spirituality.</li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0139134/\" target=\"_blank\">Cruel Intentions</a></span><br /> Vampire. How bored Toreadors (or their Ghouls) can be manipulative, abusive, horrible monsters; using and consuming others in their quest for entertainment and revenge. An allegory for the politics and boons within the Camarilla in general, and differing/changing Humanity.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0116353/\" target=\"_blank\">Foxfire</a><br /> Werewolf. Anruth, Black Fury / Kinfolk themes with a little Rite of Passage.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0116341/\" target=\"_blank\">Forest Warrior</a><br /> Werewolf. Bear with me here... this movie is basically terrible, but if you look at it as if it is a pack of cubs who find a totem of the wilderness, it suddenly becomes great for a laugh. You can peg Tribe and Auspice stereotypes to each of the kids. And keep in mind, if Werewolves are changing around puberty, the Nation is full of teens and pre-teens like this. (And suddenly the stupid problems of the Nation make so much more sense...)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><