yxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:24:48-07:00","id":701168,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce are the Wamphyri from Necroscope. The Gangrel are the Near Dark vamps. The Ventrue are the Bela Lugosi Dracula's. The Toreadors are Interview with the Vampire vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:57:33-07:00","id":701183,"title":"","content":"I don't know that <i>Near Dark</i> screams Gangrel to me (lacking the shapechanging that is their signature trait), though I imagine it strongly influenced how nomadic Sabbat packs have been written up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T12:22:57-07:00","id":701217,"title":"","content":"You can't go by powers. There are tons of vampires who don't have any powers beyond enhanced physicality. There are tons of vampires in fiction whose powers begin and end with something like +2 to +4 to all physicals, and the ability to heal between one and four health levels a round without spending blood. Flavor is a much better way of determining which vamp belongs in which clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T18:17:29-07:00","id":701487,"title":"","content":"What movies/comics would you guys recommend to get a feel for the Euthanatos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T16:36:36-07:00","id":703964,"title":"","content":"Blade- needs more mentioning here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Frailty- I completely agree is the greatest Hunter Movie ever. Incredible film. <br /> Fight Club- being the second best Hunter Movie ever (but one of the best films ever), with Tyler Durton being a great example of any of the creeeds (but not the hermits) at an Extremist level.<br /> Pretty much everything already mentioned here.<br /> Dark city and the crow and Pans Labyrinth for definite.<br /> And I'm going to go out and say Boondock Saints is also a great CWoD film. With me leaning towards the Brothers being Celestial Chorus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T20:04:05-07:00","id":704193,"title":"","content":"I know this isn't a tv show or a movie, but I've been playing the Witcher 3, and with all the werewolves and vampires in it, as well as the amazing setting, I can't help but be reminded of all the excellent Dark Ages books when playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T03:13:44-07:00","id":704616,"title":"","content":"Seanan McGuire's '<i>October Daye</i>' series reads <i>exactly</i> like <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, with a couple of house rules thrown in. Actually, the whole thing sounds like she took her sidhe wilder from a <i>Changeling</i> campaign, aged her up ten-fifteen years, and started writing novels about her new adventures as a grump.<br /> <br /> Also good for <i>Changeling</i> are movies like <b>Drop Dead Fred</b> or <b>Don't Look Under the Bed</b>, which are basically the story of a high Banality changeling (forced back Asleep and into forgetfulness) remembering that all of those childhood fantasies were &quot;real&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=701487#post701487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What movies/comics would you guys recommend to get a feel for the Euthanatos?</div> </div> </div> </div>The recent Christopher Nolan/<i>Dark Knight </i>Batman trilogy of movies aren't bad, for a look at the Euthanatos. We were actually playing around with this idea in the &quot;Are the Nephandi Truly Evil&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Bruce Wayne and Ra's al Ghul showcase the two major &quot;idealistic&quot; strains in the Euthanatos. The whole Batman persona is a classic Euthanatos tactic - removing the evil and corrupt, so that good might flourish in Gotham. Ra's al Ghul, meanwhile, is an extremist/exterminationalist Euthanatos . . . but still an idealist, in his own way. He believes that Gotham is irrevocably corrupt, and must be destroyed. However, in doing so, something good/healthy can take its place, growing from the ashes of the destroyed city.<br /> <br /> The Heath Ledger take on the Joker makes for an <i>excellent</i> Nephandus. Talia and Bane, meanwhile, are . . . &quot;pragmatic&quot; members of the Euthanatos. They want to kill Bruce Wayne, and destroy his precious city, as revenge for the death of Ra's al Ghul. But with the recent turnaround in the city's fortunes . . . they can't justify moving openly against him (or Gotham). That's what the whole revolt/nuclear device plot was about - covering their asses, for when the White Hand (the Euthanatos equivalent of Internal Affairs) starts asking questions. If there's an &quot;accidental&quot; nuclear detonation, or the citizens &quot;choose&quot; to set it off - that's proof they were too corrupt to live, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:59:17-07:00","id":705188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=704616#post704616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seanan McGuire's '<i>October Daye</i>' series reads <i>exactly</i> like <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, with a couple of house rules thrown in. Actually, the whole thing sounds like she took her sidhe wilder from a <i>Changeling</i> campaign, aged her up ten-fifteen years, and started writing novels about her new adventures as a grump.<br /> <br /> Also good for <i>Changeling</i> are movies like <b>Drop Dead Fred</b> or <b>Don't Look Under the Bed</b>, which are basically the story of a high Banality changeling (forced back Asleep and into forgetfulness) remembering that all of those childhood fantasies were &quot;real&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> The recent Christopher Nolan/<i>Dark Knight </i>Batman trilogy of movies aren't bad, for a look at the Euthanatos. We were actually playing around with this idea in the &quot;Are the Nephandi Truly Evil&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Bruce Wayne and Ra's al Ghul showcase the two major &quot;idealistic&quot; strains in the Euthanatos. The whole Batman persona is a classic Euthanatos tactic - removing the evil and corrupt, so that good might flourish in Gotham. Ra's al Ghul, meanwhile, is an extremist/exterminationalist Euthanatos . . . but still an idealist, in his own way. He believes that Gotham is irrevocably corrupt, and must be destroyed. However, in doing so, something good/healthy can take its place, growing from the ashes of the destroyed city.<br /> <br /> The Heath Ledger take on the Joker makes for an <i>excellent</i> Nephandus. Talia and Bane, meanwhile, are . . . &quot;pragmatic&quot; members of the Euthanatos. They want to kill Bruce Wayne, and destroy his precious city, as revenge for the death of Ra's al Ghul. But with the recent turnaround in the city's fortunes . . . they can't justify moving openly against him (or Gotham). That's what the whole revolt/nuclear device plot was about - covering their asses, for when the White Hand (the Euthanatos equivalent of Internal Affairs) starts asking questions. If there's an &quot;accidental&quot; nuclear detonation, or the citizens &quot;choose&quot; to set it off - that's proof they were too corrupt to live, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>.. i hate saying this, but Wanted is an excelent outlook on the Euthanathos being manipulated within, and to become &quot;Agents of Justice&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T12:18:15-07:00","id":705626,"title":"","content":"<b>Dog Soldiers</b>, set in Scotland and about a werewolf pack hunting a group of soldiers. This is absolutely the movie I recommend to get idea of a Black Spiral Dancer family being hidden in the woods. And yes, BSDs. If you've seen the movie, you know why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:08:26-07:00","id":706981,"title":"","content":"<b>The Ultimate Solution of Grace Quigley </b>is a great movie to get a feel for the Euthanatos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T03:56:04-07:00","id":712149,"title":"","content":"Hannibal (the nbc series) for Vampire <br /> Gargoyles for mage or vampire <br /> Book of Eli <br /> The last exorcism <br /> The Grey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8705-slatezymur","name":"SlateZymur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T14:52:05-07:00","id":713060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=701487#post701487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What movies/comics would you guys recommend to get a feel for the Euthanatos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, and Light Yagami from <b>Death Note</b> (manga or anime) is a good example of a Euthanatos falling to Hubris. The metaphysics of the series are different, but its still worth a look. Initially, Light was only going to use his death magic to kill one person, a kidnapper who was holding a bunch of people hostage. Then, emboldened by his success, he starts to use it to kill the worst of the worst: serial killers, war criminals, <i>et al</i> . . . who've escaped justice. All things a good Euthanatos could justify. <br /> <br /> But then he's hanging out with a demon. He starts killing cops, guilty of nothing more than trying to figure out the &quot;Kira murders&quot; (i.e. the people Light has killed). He ropes the women in his life into meddling with black magic (and also commit murder) . . . <br /> <br /> None of which is acceptable to the Euthanatos . . . but all of which are recognized temptations inherent in their paradigm. And as representatives of the White Hand (L, followed by Near and Mellow) come to investigate, Light falls even further from the path . . . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:13:52-07:00","id":713081,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a live action series about Vampire that horrendously ruined the clan lore? Such as making the Brujah sophisticated aristocrats, or the Gangrel loyal servants to the Prince?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:10:43-07:00","id":713147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=713081#post713081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a live action series about Vampire that horrendously ruined the clan lore? Such as making the Brujah sophisticated aristocrats, or the Gangrel loyal servants to the Prince?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was called <i>Kindred: The Embraced</i>, and it was terrible (thank Aaron Spelling--at least he didn't put Tori in it though). Vampires could walk around in daylight if they'd just fed (like, any vampire, not just vampires that should have Fort); the Toreador Primogen clearly had Protean 4 (which isn't unheard of, but, <i>c'mon now</i>); there was no mention of the Tremere or Sabbat <i>whatsoever; </i>Malkavians (as I recall) were treated the way mages treat marauders (i.e., hunted and killed as a matter of course); the only independent clan that ever made any appearance were the Assamites (and even then, it was basically limited to a tiny, lily white chick in a black turtleneck with a knife); the word Camarilla is never said.<br /> <br /> That having been said, the show is a freakin'<b> treasure trove</b> of TV character actors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:28:27-07:00","id":713291,"title":"","content":"Game of thrones politics for Vampire. &quot;Oh look the one really good honorable guy we all like of note has been promoted...oh..his heads been cut off. Quick everyone launch your plans now to get his stuff...everyones stuff!....all the Stuff!! While I look amazing and sleep with everyone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T08:48:11-07:00","id":729043,"title":"","content":"Looks like all the good ones have been taken already, so let me throw out some outliers.<br /> <br /> <b>Warehouse 13: </b> definitely NOT dark, but still a good show for how to run a good Son of Ether-heavy game. A group of government agents are transferred to a mysterious off-the-books warehouse in South Dakota where they hunt down &quot;Artifacts&quot;, items of special significance and power that either belonged to famous/brilliant/infamous people that either BECAME mystical in nature by virture of their owner OR is responsible for some of the more unbelievable things they're owners were reputed to have done. It's VERY modern steampunk. Hell, HG Wells even shows up to become a recurring frenemy throughout the run of the show. The series ran for five seasons, got an actual ending, and is available in a surprisingly cheap box set. It's also on Netflix.<br /> <br /> <b>The Originals: </b> this is a good show for getting a handle on vampire elders, despite how very NOT-WoD it's setting is. It's also a good example of how to run a crossover show. The main cast are centered around the family of first vampires, and the fact that they've settled in New Orleans. The existing factions of vampires, werewolves, witches, and humans are NOT happy, and it's basically an on-going battle of who controls the city over the backdrop of personal drama and private agendas. <br /> <br /> Their big advantage is true immortality. Only weapons made of a certain white oak could kill them, and like sensible protagonists, they burned that sucker down the second they figured it out. So they cannot be killed by most known means. The only known weapons that hurt them are a set of enchanted silver daggers that send them into torpor if stabbed in the heart. People have complained about it ruining the drama, but I like that the standard Main Character Shield is actually acknowledged in-universe, complete with rules and exceptions (they were a family of 5, they're down to 3).<br /> <br /> This third season has become more WoD-like as they've introduced the concept of Sire-Lines (not-clans of vampires, each descended from a different member of said family) that are at war with each other, and a society of snobby vampires who like to manipulate history for their advantage, called the Strix (I shouted REALLY?! when that name was dropped; seriously I think the CW may owe Onyx Path some royalties for this). The biggest problem with the series (to me, at least) is that there are no consistent rules for magic. If there's a rule established, a &quot;loop hole&quot; will be found later on down the road, and it's basically used as a giant Plot Device with no internal consistency or limits. One episode, it's basically True Magick, limited only by the available power source and will of the caster. Next episode, it's bog standard hedge magic that's weak, easily thwartable, and incapable of doing anything without long involved rituals and chants.<br /> <br /> First two seasons are on Netflix. Season 3 airs on the CW.<br /> <br /> <b>Hemlock Grove: Netflix Original Series </b>I'm going to recommend this show, despite not liking it personally. Basically think Vampire Diaries meets Twin Peaks with a slight Technocratic bent. All the classic monster types (vampire, werewolf, gypsy magic, frankenstein's monster) are represented, though in some unusual ways, there's a lot of dark science in the background, and there are even witch-hunters. I recommend Season 1 as a good murder mystery set in the World of Darkness. It's also a good example of how to run a Neonate level crossover game. I can't go into too many details without major spoilers. It's only twelve episodes, and things move. I don't recommend Season 2, however. But that's personal bias.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural:</b> Surprised I didn't see this on a quick scan of the previous pages, but I'll mention. Basically, follow a pair of brothers as they hunt down monsters through the American Midwest. It actually avoids overusing the traditional baddies (vampires, werewolves, etc), and has focused on more obscure creatures for the most part. Later, demons and angels take a larger focus. LONG-running CW show, currently on Season 11. <u><i><b> DO NOT WATCH PAST SEASON FIVE.</b></i></u> It was the planned ending of the show. Original showrunner left after that, and it shows. I won't say the later seasons are terrible (okay, Season Seven was awful). There are good episodes every season, and seasonal metaplots are usually solid, but the character arcs have become dry and repetitive, and the stand-alone episodes feel like padding, rather than expanding on the mythology of the setting. It's clear they're out of ideas, but the CW won't let it die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:33:03-07:00","id":735028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=729043#post729043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supernatural:</b> Surprised I didn't see this on a quick scan of the previous pages, but I'll mention. Basically, follow a pair of brothers as they hunt down monsters through the American Midwest. It actually avoids overusing the traditional baddies (vampires, werewolves, etc), and has focused on more obscure creatures for the most part. Later, demons and angels take a larger focus. LONG-running CW show, currently on Season 11. <u><i><b> DO NOT WATCH PAST SEASON FIVE.</b></i></u> It was the planned ending of the show. Original showrunner left after that, and it shows. I won't say the later seasons are terrible (okay, Season Seven was awful). There are good episodes every season, and seasonal metaplots are usually solid, but the character arcs have become dry and repetitive, and the stand-alone episodes feel like padding, rather than expanding on the mythology of the setting. It's clear they're out of ideas, but the CW won't let it die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I liked the return to form of some of the follow-up seasons (the filler has been some of my favorite stuff, because honestly I just want a monster of the week procedural with little overarching plot). And Season 11 has me excited again in a way that 9 and 10 didn't.<br /> <br /> Kind of hoping it ends after the current arc is resolved though. It's got a &quot;Finally, for real this time guys&quot; vibe to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my own contribution to this thread:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0CB4QFjAAahUKEwi_n8jzy-XIAhWFND4KHb5kDzA&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.telltalegames.com%2Fthewolfamongus%2F&amp;usg=AFQjCNHDTJJhXARjl6HzWAG1SMpXsfzdmw&amp;sig2=TUbOjizrZgo-ibwb-n3bDQ\" target=\"_blank\">A Wolf Among Us</a>:</b> It feels like a well-done vampire city: established hierarchy, clearly-defined chain of command, classist overtones. Bigby's obviously a powerful Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:51:14-07:00","id":735052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=735028#post735028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I liked the return to form of some of the follow-up seasons (the filler has been some of my favorite stuff, because honestly I just want a monster of the week procedural with little overarching plot). And Season 11 has me excited again in a way that 9 and 10 didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried watching Supernatural, but a story cannot survive on daddy issues alone.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on &quot;honestly I just want a monster of the week procedural with little overarching plot&quot;. I mean, I loved Babylon 5 and Battlestar Galactica, but sometimes I just want to watch a 44-minute story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:10:19-07:00","id":745544,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:48px\">ASH VS THE EVIL DEAD.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">if youre not watching it, then leave the forums and Do watch it NOW!</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:28:05-08:00","id":747091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=735028#post735028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I liked the return to form of some of the follow-up seasons (the filler has been some of my favorite stuff, because honestly I just want a monster of the week procedural with little overarching plot). And Season 11 has me excited again in a way that 9 and 10 didn't.<br /> <br /> Kind of hoping it ends after the current arc is resolved though. It's got a &quot;Finally, for real this time guys&quot; vibe to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my own contribution to this thread:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0CB4QFjAAahUKEwi_n8jzy-XIAhWFND4KHb5kDzA&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.telltalegames.com%2Fthewolfamongus%2F&amp;usg=AFQjCNHDTJJhXARjl6HzWAG1SMpXsfzdmw&amp;sig2=TUbOjizrZgo-ibwb-n3bDQ\" target=\"_blank\">A Wolf Among Us</a>:</b> It feels like a well-done vampire city: established hierarchy, clearly-defined chain of command, classist overtones. Bigby's obviously a powerful Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would agree with you, except the brothers' character arcs have stopped dead, and they do nothing but repeat the same notes OVER AND OVER AND OVER again. I prefer the standalone &quot;strange&quot; episodes, where it ditches the horror for Raimi-esque comedy and leaning heavily on the Fourth Wall. Or better yet, the most recent episode, where it's basically a Monster of the Week tale, told from the perspective of the Impala, so to speak. It also was one of the few times in the last few years where we've gotten to see the brothers relax, have fun, and act like human beings, something the show has SORELY lacked for a while now. It's also nice to have an episode where the brothers aren't actively concealing Big Truths from each other, the revelation of which drives them apart for a few episodes. I'm so sick of that, I could scream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:42:05-08:00","id":747627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=747091#post747091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would agree with you, except the brothers' character arcs have stopped dead, and they do nothing but repeat the same notes OVER AND OVER AND OVER again. I prefer the standalone &quot;strange&quot; episodes, where it ditches the horror for Raimi-esque comedy and leaning heavily on the Fourth Wall. Or better yet, the most recent episode, where it's basically a Monster of the Week tale, told from the perspective of the Impala, so to speak. It also was one of the few times in the last few years where we've gotten to see the brothers relax, have fun, and act like human beings, something the show has SORELY lacked for a while now. It's also nice to have an episode where the brothers aren't actively concealing Big Truths from each other, the revelation of which drives them apart for a few episodes. I'm so sick of that, I could scream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the sad thing is I could see this coming back in the third season when the frontrunner was still on board. The writers basically circle jerked to the demon plot line to the point where the story started to get tiresome and the monster of the week episodes were the only relief as you got to a see a little more of the Supernatural universe and what it contained. The show's original premise was basically &quot;Brothers hunting monsters together&quot; and twisted into &quot;Brothers dealing with whatever big bad plot line is bearing down on them while occasionally fighting monsters.&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:32:14-08:00","id":751395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=747627#post747627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the sad thing is I could see this coming back in the third season when the frontrunner was still on board. The writers basically circle jerked to the demon plot line to the point where the story started to get tiresome and the monster of the week episodes were the only relief as you got to a see a little more of the Supernatural universe and what it contained. The show's original premise was basically &quot;Brothers hunting monsters together&quot; and twisted into &quot;Brothers dealing with whatever big bad plot line is bearing down on them while occasionally fighting monsters.&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the big bad plotlines, the problem is the writers have no sense of pacing. After Season 5, you can literally just watch &quot;The first 2-3 episodes of the season, the two middle episodes that form the mid-season cliffhanger for the holiday hiatus, and the final 2-3 episodes of the season&quot; and miss NOTHING but the same, tired stale character arcs and repetitive MoW filler. They'd honestly be better served going down to a 12 episode season like the BBC. ... Hell, most American shows would be better served by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:32:48-08:00","id":751400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=745544#post745544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\">ASH VS THE EVIL DEAD.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">if youre not watching it, then leave the forums and Do watch it NOW!</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have Starz. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:01:35-08:00","id":751463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=745544#post745544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\">ASH VS THE EVIL DEAD.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">if youre not watching it, then leave the forums and Do watch it NOW!</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This...I...I didn't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:22:31-08:00","id":751482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=751463#post751463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This...I...I didn't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Youre dead to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T01:26:38-08:00","id":753375,"title":"","content":"Just recently started Kristen Painter's <i>House of Comarre</i> series, which plays out much like a Vampire, Hunter, and Demon crossover (obviously not all on the same side). The female lead, Chrysabelle, is a comarre - basically an incredibly valuable feeding slave, specifically bred/trained/tattooed to remind the elite of vampire society of the sun. But when her master turns up murdered, and she's the prime suspect, she flees . . .and becomes a key pawn in a scheme to free the Fallen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amazon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Born into a life of secrets and service, Chrysabelle's body bears the telltale marks of a comarr\u00e9 -- a special race of humans bred to feed vampire nobility. When her patron is murdered, she becomes the prime suspect, which sends her running into the mortal world...and into the arms of Malkolm, an outcast vampire cursed to kill every being from whom he drinks.<br /> <br /> Now, Chrysabelle and Malkolm must work together to stop a plot to merge the mortal and supernatural worlds. If they fail, a chaos unlike anything anyone has ever seen will threaten to reign.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't comarre in the World of Darkness, but the author's setting is similar, and with the occasional hint that she's familiar with <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i><br /> <br /> And on the live action front - TNT's <b>Witchblade </b>is gorgeous. Corrupt cops, an occult conspiracy dating back to Nazi Germany, demonic priests . . . Not to mention that most of the fights took place under the influence of the Witchblade, turning each battle into a surreal allegory. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this adaptation of the Top Cow comic book, Witchblade is the story of a New York detective, Sara &quot;Pez&quot; Pezzini, whose search for justice brings her into contact with the Witchblade, an ancient, intelligent, living weapon so powerful it can battle Earth's darkest evil forces. Week in and week out, &quot;Pez&quot; employs her skills as a police detective to fight crime. She finds she must employ the Witchblade to combat a much greater and frighteningly organized conspiracy of evil that threatens the very soul of humanity. As Sara tries to keep the secret of the Witchblade, do her job and have a personal life, she finds that her most formidable adversary may be the Witchblade itself. </div> </div> </div>Spike TV's live action <b>Blade</b> tv series is excellent, too. They couldn't get Wesley Snipes to play Blade . . . but I think his replacement is 10x better in the role of the half-vampire. Much of the action revolves around Blade getting a newly turned vampire to &quot;go undercover&quot; for him, allowing the series to focus a lot on vampiric society<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T02:40:41-08:00","id":753481,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Welcome to Night Vale--It's neither a movie nor TV show, but a podcast pretending to be a community radio program. It is great fodder for any WoD game. It's not nearly as subtle (or serious) as the WoD, but the ideas can be tweaked and toned down. It's kind of like if all the weirdness in the World of Darkness was out in the open. Pretty much all the standard conspiracies are real in Night Vale, plus a whole lot of original ones.<br /> <br /> It's free on iTunes and Youtube.</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;The Summer Reading Program for children and teens has begun at the Night Vale Public Library. This comes as an alarming surprise, given that the program was abolished by the City Council thirty years ago. Though parents and teenagers have asked on several occasions to reinstate the program, the City Council has maintained its position, citing lack of taxpayer funds, the extreme danger posed by books, the peril of exposing children to librarians, and of course, the incident that precipitated the ban, which the town\u2019s older residents will refer to only as \u201cThe Time Of Knives\u201d.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:31:13-08:00","id":754214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=753375#post753375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And on the live action front - TNT's <b>Witchblade </b>is gorgeous. Corrupt cops, an occult conspiracy dating back to Nazi Germany, demonic priests . . . Not to mention that most of the fights took place under the influence of the Witchblade, turning each battle into a surreal allegory.<br /> <br /> Spike TV's live action <b>Blade</b> tv series is excellent, too. They couldn't get Wesley Snipes to play Blade . . . but I think his replacement is 10x better in the role of the half-vampire. Much of the action revolves around Blade getting a newly turned vampire to &quot;go undercover&quot; for him, allowing the series to focus a lot on vampiric society</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, it's been a while since I've seen Witchblade. Good series, especially Season 1. Season 2 had its... quirks, but was solid overall. Unfortunately, the lead's substance abuse problems brought a premature end to the show. <br /> <br /> Blade the Series was surprisingly good, and fans might have noticed the antagonist, Marcus Van Sciver, having moved to Sleepy Hollow to play the head-attached version of the Headless Horseman of Death in flashbacks and the odd mystical encounter. Honestly, it was ahead of it's time. Given that Marvel's gotten the rights to the franchise back, I'm hoping they'll do a Netflix series. I'd prefer it continue where the old one left off, but that's impractical. I imagine they'll reboot the franchise to go better with the MCU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:21:01-08:00","id":755079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=753375#post753375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>but I think his replacement is 10x better in the role of the half-vampire.</b> Much of the action revolves around Blade getting a newly turned vampire to &quot;go undercover&quot; for him, allowing the series to focus a lot on vampiric society</div> </div> </div> </div>You think Sticky Fingaz did a better job as Blade than Wesley Snipes?<br /> <br /> I...I can't...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:00:36-08:00","id":756572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=755079#post755079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think Sticky Fingaz did a better job as Blade than Wesley Snipes?<br /> <br /> I...I can't...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on the movie. Snipes was good in the first two, but terrible in the third.<br /> <br /> The TV actor did a good job with a different take on the character. Honestly, it felt more like a reboot than a continuation, and ties to the film trilogy were very sparse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:54:43-08:00","id":757868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=756572#post756572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the movie. Snipes was good in the first two, but terrible in the third.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Snipes' movie lobby cardboard cut-out would have done as good a job as he did in <i>Blade: Trinity</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, while I wasn't a fan of Sticky in the role, I did like the series as a whole. Let's face it, Jill Wagner was playing the protagonist in all but name, and doing a great job of it. And Charlotte was at least the best villain in the franchise since Deacon Frost.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:46:16-08:00","id":758041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=753481#post753481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Welcome to Night Vale--It's neither a movie nor TV show, but a podcast pretending to be a community radio program. It is great fodder for any WoD game. It's not nearly as subtle (or serious) as the WoD, but the ideas can be tweaked and toned down. It's kind of like if all the weirdness in the World of Darkness was out in the open. Pretty much all the standard conspiracies are real in Night Vale, plus a whole lot of original ones.<br /> <br /> It's free on iTunes and Youtube.</span></span> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>It a book now, too! <b>Welcome to Night Vale</b> just came out in hardcover:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amazon.com</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Located in a nameless desert somewhere in the great American Southwest, Night Vale is a small town where ghosts, angels, aliens, and government conspiracies are all commonplace parts of everyday life. It is here that the lives of two women, with two mysteries, will converge.<br /> <br /> Nineteen-year-old Night Vale pawn shop owner Jackie Fierro is given a paper marked &quot;KING CITY&quot; by a mysterious man in a tan jacket holding a deer skin suitcase. Everything about him and his paper unsettles her, especially the fact that she can't seem to get the paper to leave her hand, and that no one who meets this man can remember anything about him. Jackie is determined to uncover the mystery of King City and the man in the tan jacket before she herself unravels.<br /> <br /> Night Vale PTA treasurer Diane Crayton's son, Josh, is moody and also a shape shifter. And lately Diane's started to see her son's father everywhere she goes, looking the same as the day he left years earlier, when they were both teenagers. Josh, looking different every time Diane sees him, shows a stronger and stronger interest in his estranged father, leading to a disaster Diane can see coming, even as she is helpless to prevent it.<br /> <br /> Diane's search to reconnect with her son and Jackie's search for her former routine life collide as they find themselves coming back to two words: &quot;KING CITY&quot;. It is King City that holds the key to both of their mysteries, and their futures...if they can ever find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:27:18-08:00","id":760215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=757868#post757868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Snipes' movie lobby cardboard cut-out would have done as good a job as he did in <i>Blade: Trinity</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, while I wasn't a fan of Sticky in the role, I did like the series as a whole. Let's face it, Jill Wagner was playing the protagonist in all but name, and doing a great job of it. And Charlotte was at least the best villain in the franchise since Deacon Frost.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't like him at first, but his sense of snark, combined with his camaraderie with both Jill Wagner and his sidekick made the show work. I felt like they were BOTH the leads, given there were two plots going on at any given time. Eh, I saw charlotte done better by Divia in Forever Knight, sorry. Marcus Van Sciver was one of the best on-screen Ventrue I've ever seen, particularly a young and ambitious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:22:21-08:00","id":761057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=760215#post760215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I saw charlotte done better by Divia in Forever Knight, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but Divia was arguably the best child vampire ever on TV (and possibly rivaled Kirsten Dunst's Claudia). Charlotte was a watered-down version, but I still liked her better than Marcus and the assorted other villains on the show, or in the 2nd and 3rd movies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:27:45-08:00","id":761222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=761057#post761057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, but Divia was arguably the best child vampire ever on TV (and possibly rivaled Kirsten Dunst's Claudia). Charlotte was a watered-down version, but I still liked her better than Marcus and the assorted other villains on the show, or in the 2nd and 3rd movies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aw, man, I LOVED Marcus. I thought he perfectly encapsulated a Ventrue ancillae. True, he was basically Prince of Detroit, but it was clear that in-House, he was no elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T19:16:29-08:00","id":762760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=713147#post713147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it was called <i>Kindred: The Embraced</i>, and it was terrible (thank Aaron Spelling--at least he didn't put Tori in it though). Vampires could walk around in daylight if they'd just fed (like, any vampire, not just vampires that should have Fort); the Toreador Primogen clearly had Protean 4 (which isn't unheard of, but, <i>c'mon now</i>); there was no mention of the Tremere or Sabbat <i>whatsoever; </i>Malkavians (as I recall) were treated the way mages treat marauders (i.e., hunted and killed as a matter of course); the only independent clan that ever made any appearance were the Assamites (and even then, it was basically limited to a tiny, lily white chick in a black turtleneck with a knife); the word Camarilla is never said..</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, a whole lot of oWoD Vampire canon/Clans/terminology was intentionally left out because Mark Rein-Hagen, White Wolf and/or copyright holders thus for Vampire: the Masquerade refused to allow Spelling to use them in Kindred: the Embraced. This is not meant to be hard detail, as what I know I picked up quite some time after the series came and went, but what I know was related to me by several local players in diffierent groups whose explanations matched evenly.<br /> <br /> The series didn't even get to double-digit episodes, but for what it's worth I'm grateful the proposed inclusion of the Garou didn't come along. I'll take Bitten (in my hometown, no less!) over that any day, thanks.<br /> <br /> -2Paw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/VSrvqCW.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5964-twopaw-tarnished-silver","name":"Twopaw Tarnished-Silver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:10:08-08:00","id":763507,"title":"","content":"Odd Thomas- Great inspiration for Second Sight and Wraith<br /> John dies at the End- Could be a Great inspirations for Hunter or Mage. ((The Cop's speech in the trailer just nails it with me))<br /> Big Trouble in Little China<br /> The Strain<br /> Nightmare on Elm St.<br /> The Lost Boys<br /> Gingersnaps<br /> Predator 1-2<br /> Push<br /> The Chronicle<br /> Ink<br /> Time Bandits<br /> Shutter-Island<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T19:45:15-08:00","id":765994,"title":"","content":"I can recommend Chloe Neil's <i>Chicagolands Vampire </i>series, particularly the first book, <b>Some Girls Bite</b>. Sort of an urban (Chicago-based) counterpart to <b>True Blood</b>, it occurs after the Masquerade comes down, and vampires admit they exist:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Some Girls Bite</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the life of a graduate student wasn't exactly glamorous, but it was Merit's. She was doing fine until a rogue vampire attacked her. But he only got a sip before he was scared away by another bloodsucker and this one decided the best way to save her life was to make her the walking undead.<br /> <br /> Turns out her savior was the master vampire of Cadogan House. Now she's traded sweating over her thesis for learning to fit in at a Hyde Park mansion full of vamps loyal to Ethan &quot;Lord o' the Manor&quot; Sullivan. Of course, as a tall, green-eyed, four-hundred- year-old vampire, he has centuries-worth of charm, but unfortunately he expects her gratitude - and servitude. But an inconvenient sunlight allergy and Ethan's attitude are the least of her concerns. Someone's still out to get her. Her initiation into Chicago's nightlife may be the first skirmish in a war and there will be blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Later volumes were a bit too . . . &quot;motivated&quot; in showing how vampires and other supernaturals get along, but they weren't bad. And the first book was <i>fun</i>, showing Merit's first days as a vampire, from her Embrace to her first big fight. The scene where she and her (human) roommate try to figure out how to drink bagged blood . . .Two grad students, hunched over the counter, poking at a bag of blood with straws. . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or if you want a <i>Hunter</i>-esque series (nWoD or classic), Larry Correia's <b>Monster Hunter International </b>is a good choice. It's basically . . . the NRA takes on the Cthulhu Mythos (&quot;We need more guns - no, the big ones!&quot; . . . &quot;Hey! Tim brought a rocket launcher!&quot; . . . &quot;Dibs on the flamethrower!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). And the author's famously said, &quot;the only reason a vampire should sparkle is if I've doused it in napalm&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Five days after Owen Zastava Pitt pushed his insufferable boss out of a fourteenth story window, he woke up in the hospital with a scarred face, an unbelievable memory, and a job offer.<br /> <br /> It turns out that monsters are real. All the things from myth, legend, and B-movies are out there, waiting in the shadows. Officially secret, some of them are evil, and some are just hungry. On the other side are the people who kill monsters for a living. Monster Hunter International is the premier eradication company in the business. And now Owen is their newest recruit.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s actually a pretty sweet gig, except for one little problem. An ancient entity known as the Cursed One has returned to settle a centuries old vendetta. Should the Cursed One succeed, it means the end of the world, and MHI is the only thing standing in his way. With the clock ticking towards Armageddon, Owen finds himself trapped between legions of undead minions, belligerent federal agents, a cryptic ghost who has taken up residence inside his head, and the cursed family of the woman he loves.<br /> <br /> Business is good . . </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> If you've ever wanted to run a <i>Hunter</i> game where the government knows about the supernatural, and is (quietly) sponsoring teams to hunt it down, <i>MHI</i> is right up your alley. Average humanity is still in the dark about the supernatural, but various mercenary firms and bounty hunters in-the-know compete for the bounties sponsored by the government. The average zombie's only worth a couple bucks, but taking down a Great Old One can net you tens of millions.<br /> <br /> Really, its quite at home in the World of Darkness. And I dare any Storytellers out there to read the series, and not want to rip off Decision Week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-14-2015, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:55:27-08:00","id":772772,"title":"","content":"Only Lovers Left Alive: this movie is a little boring but great fodder for clan toreador's quiet moments and a great look at the clan's mind set. <br /> <br /> Once Upon Time: this show IS Changeling: The Dreaming<br /> <br /> The Vampire Diaries and the Originals: No seriously want to know how neonates and elders work politics and intrigue? CHeck out these shows.<br /> <br /> American Horror Story: <br /> <br /> Murder House: Great Wraith and Hunter Fodder<br /> <br /> Asylum: probably better for New World of Darkness Changeling and Hunter but still good material for Demon The Fallen<br /> <br /> Coven: despite its flaws actually a pretty look at chantry spats and inter tradition feuds<br /> <br /> Freak show: not so much....yeah lets just skip this one (though Twisty was still pretty awesome)<br /> <br /> Hotel: The Countess is a good look at just how evil and terrifying a Toreador (or antitribu) can be, and Sally and the Addiction Demon make a great look at a Wraith and her Shadow<br /> <br /> Gotham: a good look at World of Darkness cities<br /> <br /> The 100: What would happen if a bunch of Void Engineers and extraordinary citizens got trapped across the Gauntlet in Pangaea?<br /> <br /> Ash vs. Evil Dead: Hunter and Demon<br /> <br /> Agents of S.H.I.E.L,D,: Technocrats as the good guys<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:25:11-08:00","id":773048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=772772#post772772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Lovers Left Alive: this movie is a little boring but great fodder for clan toreador's quiet moments and a great look at the clan's mind set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also it shows why you should never embrace your kid sister.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=772772#post772772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once Upon Time: this show IS Changeling: The Dreaming</div> </div> </div> </div>OMFG. How did I not notice this before!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:03:16-08:00","id":778582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=60615#post60615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just started watching a canadian produced werewolf show called Bitten that just started airing. It's not as kitchy as Teen Wolf, but there's not too much material yet for me to make a judgement. So far though it looks promising. I can definitely watch it for a season. It takes itself a bit seriously, but not too seriously. The dynamics between pack members are believable. There's even some that stand out as clear Auspices. Only 3 episodes in and I'm taking one character's death pretty personally. (DAMNIT WHYYYYY?!! I LIKED THAT ONE CHARACTER who's name I can't remember yet because the show is so new.... *snuffle* damnit...) Anyways, it looks like it's gonna be good WoD fodder. The werewolves only change into one form that's clearly CG but you can tell they worked hard on the Mo-cap to get it as close as they can. And CG fur is F-ing HARD. So kudos for the show's producers. I hope this one sticks around for a few seasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd reccomend dearly the books, written by Kelley Armstrong. They have some really, really nice vibe to them that unfortunatedly (for me, maybe because i really like the books) is lost in the series.If it continues long enough, we will see unfold some really cool stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:05:36-08:00","id":778618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58519-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-movies-and-tv-shows?p=772772#post772772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotham: a good look at World of Darkness cities<br /> <br /> The 100: What would happen if a bunch of Void Engineers and extraordinary citizens got trapped across the Gauntlet in Pangaea?<br /> <br /> Ash vs. Evil Dead: Hunter and Demon<br /> <br /> Agents of S.H.I.E.L,D,: Technocrats as the good guys<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Couple of good recommendations I need to watch.<br /> <br /> For anyone who tried Gotham and loathed it (like I did; watched half of Season 1, quit and refused to go back until roommate called in a favor), Season 2 is MUCH MUCH better. It's still ... campy, but it's found it's footing, made its characters likable, and there's a sense of consistency and direction that Season 1 lacked. Also, of the two worst characters, one is gone, and one has gone insane and become a villain, so VAST improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"